[Music]  running into an invisible wall is one of  the most annoying things that can happen  in an open world game but such  boundaries don't always have to be so  boring and obvious here are 10 of the  coolest weirdest almost over-the-top  methods open-world games have used to  keep players contained number 10 the  Elder Scrolls online a swarm of piranhas  despite initial appearances the world of  Tamriel does have its limits whilst  oblivion and Skyrim simply showed a  message on screen telling you to go back  the other way the Elder Scrolls online  takes a slightly snappier approach and  in that you get devoured by piranhas if  you swim too far off the coast it's kind  of nasty number 9 gothic an electric  dome from biting piranhas to piranha  bytes the German developer known for  making an unforgiving alternative to the  Elder Scrolls games in its own series  gothic I am NOT interested in who you  are the first gothic game encased its  prison world in a giant dome forcefield  as a part of the story which also  happened to function nicely as an  electrical barrier I can be near number  eight far cry to a sudden malaria attack  famous for being one of the few  first-person shooters that beat you down  at every opportunity far cry 2 extended  this philosophy to the edges of its open  savanna causing you to suffer a sudden  and intense malaria attack if you stray  too far off the beaten track collapsing  into the fetal position isn't exactly  the standard shooter power fantasy but  in Far Cry 2 you take what you get  number 7 World of Warcraft the guardian  of Blizzard World of Warcraft entices  players to venture off and explore its  colorful nooks and crannies but for  areas that weren't actually built for  players Blizzard needed a high-level  enemy to keep them out this was the  guardian of Blizzard a massive elemental  golem that could kill anyone in one hit  and it could be spawned by GM's  elsewhere if anyone was making a ruckus  number 6 Grand Theft Auto for an instant  6 star wanted level Grand Theft Auto 4  divided Liberty City into a series of  islands closing them off from one  another with police roadblocks  major bridges but there's always another  way around especially if you're not  opposed to going for a swim  however passing the block' results in an  instant six star wanted level with  police shutting down the city until the  offending Explorer is brought to justice  number five Unreal Tournament 2004 the  ion cannon but bigger maps and a lot of  vehicles to drive around in them Unreal  Tournament 2004 needed a way to keep  players boxed into its arena levels that  its predecessor didn't have so it took  last year's super weapon the ion cannon  and made its orbiting satellite  automatically lock on and vaporize any  players who double jump outside the maps  boundaries  personally I'd have just taken - then  with a flat cannon but each to their own  number for Serious Sam 3 BF a a giant  sand worm the Serious Sam series is  known for its expansive levels but the  third entry did away with the boxed  canyons and walled plazas of the  previous games in favour of a completely  open desert so it's only appropriate  that a gigantic sand worm pops up and  swallows anyone who spies a mirage and  goes off wondering if this would you can  there'd be a dick joke somewhere in here  number three Just Cause two the road to  nowhere heading to a certain boundary in  Just Cause twos islands of Pinal reveals  just why developers need to keep players  boxed in here the world simply ends its  like someone has taken a buzzsaw to the  geometry unfortunately pronounced  drivers don't seem to realize this and  will drive off the edge forever like  some kind of road to nowhere  number two Motocross Madness an  invisible bike Canon the wide-open stunt  for ease of Motocross Madness were  surrounded by near vertical cliffs but  thanks to 1998 wonky driving physics you  could will be your way straight up them  now the developers thought ahead and  caused any clever rider to really launch  back into the level by way of a giant  invisible Canon qs flat sound in three  one number one crisis shark attack and  battleship crisis takes the top spot for  having more than one way to kill its  wandering players if you maximum jump  off the islands white shores and maximum  swim out into the depths you're  eventually gonna get eaten by a shark  but if you get smart and dodged this guy  on a boat  the North Korean battleships on the  horizon will sink you with a  heat-seeking torpedo not even a nano  suits maximum armor is going to deflect  one of those

